ets_2020-11-13","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:867996158:2655","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_043.bib.mrc:170077303:3878"],"title":"Zen-Brain reflections","dewey_decimal_class":["294.3/422"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"identifiers":{"librarything":["1161733"],"goodreads":["238879"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["2005052046"],"subjects":["Meditation -- Zen Buddhism -- Psysiological aspects.","Meditation -- Zen Buddhism -- Psychology.","Consciousness -- Religious aspects -- Zen Buddhism.","Zen Buddhism."],"publish_date":"2006","publish_country":"mau","by_statement":"James H. Austin.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2687558W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:O6-AXX-878","urn:bwbsku:W3-CXS-204"],"oclc_numbers":["61229817"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"This sequel to the widely read Zen and the Brain continues James Austin's explorations into the key interrelationships between Zen Buddhism and brain research. In Zen-Brain Reflections, Austin, a clinical neurologist, researcher, and Zen practitioner, examines the evolving psychological processes and brain changes associated with the path of long-range meditative training. Austin draws not only on the latest neuroscience research and new neuroimaging studies but also on Zen literature and his personal experience with alternate states of consciousness. Zen-Brain Reflections takes up where the earlier book left off. It addresses such questions as: how do placebos and acupuncture change the brain? Can neuroimaging studies localize the sites where our notions of self arise? How can the latest brain imaging methods monitor meditators more effectively? How do long years of meditative training plus brief enlightened states produce pivotal transformations in the physiology of the brain? In many chapters testable hypotheses suggest ways to correlate normal brain functions and meditative training with the phenomena of extraordinary states of consciousness.\"--Jacket."},"number_of_pages":586,"latest_revision":15,"revision":15,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-07-11T00:04:46.090487"}}},"ISBN:9780060957544":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780060957544","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7285622M/Not_Always_So","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7285622M/Not_Always_So","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/42123-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Harper Paperbacks"],"number_of_pages":176,"subtitle":"Practicing the True Spirit of Zen","covers":[42123],"lc_classifications":["BQ928.S997"],"key":"/books/OL7285622M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL27128A","name":"Shunryū Suzuki"},{"key":"/authors/OL361965A","name":"Edward Espe Brown"},{"key":"/authors/OL2631340A","name":"Zen Center San Francisco"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["bwb:9780060957544"],"title":"Not Always So","identifiers":{"librarything":["86205"],"goodreads":["238843"]},"isbn_13":["9780060957544"],"isbn_10":["0060957549"],"publish_date":"May 27, 2003","oclc_numbers":["53236140"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL14960913W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Shikantaza, our zazen, is just to be ourselves."},"latest_revision":10,"revision":10,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-11-29T03:55:53.126538"}}},"ISBN:9780060197858":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780060197858","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7275964M/Not_Always_So","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7275964M/Not_Always_So","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/23354-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["HarperCollins"],"number_of_pages":176,"subtitle":"Practicing the True Spirit of Zen","covers":[23354],"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223060403160","urn:sfpl:31223060860203","urn:sfpl:31223060547818","urn:sfpl:31223060547891","urn:sfpl:31223066452187","urn:sfpl:31223060547826","urn:sfpl:31223060547842","urn:sfpl:31223060547925"],"key":"/books/OL7275964M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL27128A","name":"Shunryū Suzuki"},{"key":"/authors/OL361965A","name":"Edward Espe Brown"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["amazon:0060197854:3:1858365746:249555","amazon:0060197854:o-2:2203006083:247224","marc:marc_loc_updates/v37.i01.records.utf8:1886068:808","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run02.mrc:247592479:2942","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part28.utf8:228326755:926","bwb:9780060197858","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-007.mrc:309802058:2850","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_009.bib.mrc:308937611:2791"],"title":"Not Always So","identifiers":{"goodreads":["2010677"],"librarything":["86205"]},"isbn_13":["9780060197858"],"isbn_10":["0060197854"],"publish_date":"May 28, 2002","works":[{"key":"/works/OL14960913W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Calmness of mind is beyond the end of your exhalation, so if you exhale smoothly, without trying to exhale, you are entering into the complete perfect calmness of your mind \""},"lccn":["2001051740"],"lc_classifications":["BQ9288 .S993 2002","BQ928.S997 2002","BQ928 . S997 2002","BQ9288 .S997 2002"],"oclc_numbers":["63159738","48449931"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Chosen and edited by Edward Espe Brown, author and student of Suzuki's, the lectures are taken from the last three years of Suzuki's life. His maturity as a teacher with a deep commitment to conveying his message is warmly and fully expressed.\".\n\n\"In Not Always So, Suzuki voices Zen in everyday language, with humor and good-heartedness. While offering sustenance much like a mother and father lending a hand, Suzuki encourages you to find your own way. Rather than emphasize specific directions and techniques, his teaching encourages you to touch and know your true heart and to express yourself fully. Suzuki's words do not seem to come from outside, but awaken a voice arising from your own being.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-07-24T21:22:40.200371"}}},"ISBN:9789522602541":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9789522602541","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL57257364M/Kirjeitä_tyhjyydestä","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL57257364M/Kirjeitä_tyhjyydestä","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14829617-S.jpg","details":{"works":[{"key":"/works/OL14960913W"}],"title":"Kirjeitä tyhjyydestä","publishers":["Basam Books"],"publish_date":"2014-01-01","key":"/books/OL57257364M","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"identifiers":{},"covers":[14829617],"isbn_13":["9789522602541"],"classifications":{"finnish_public_libraries_classification_system":["29.53","17.3"]},"subtitle":"Zen ja elämisen taito","publish_places":["Helsinki, Finland"],"contributors":[{"role":"Author name as appears on this edition","name":"Shunryū Suzuki"},{"role":"Translator","name":"Lauri Proceddu"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/fin"}],"translation_of":"Not always so","translated_from":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Tämä on ihastuttava kokoelma kauniita, syvällisiä, hienostelemattomia ja lyhyitä zenpuheita. Suzukin opetus korostaa maailmassa olemista. Hän ei aja takaa erityistä, yhtäkkistä valaistumistapahtumaa. Hän puhuu kokemusperäisen valaistumisen puolesta, joka antaa merkitystä kokonaisvaltaiselle läsnäololle nykyhetkessä: valaistuminen on mahdollista laittaessasi ruokaa tai pyyhkiessäsi pölyjä. Suzukin opetukset kehkeytyvät yksinkertaisista tarinoista, yleensä hänen omista kokemuksistaan. Kirja on lähes täysin vapa